    "w130": { "explanation": "Fuerint can be future perfect indicative or perfect subjunctive in form. With inebriati it presents a resulting state of drunkenness in the steward’s description of a general custom, not an assertion about these wedding guests. The plural drinkers are the understood subject. English “when the guests have become drunk” expresses the sequence without deciding the Latin mood." },
